ression`, chart_relationship_title: `Relationship Health`, wage_warning: `Wage offer must be between 0% and 15%`, safety_warning: `Safety investment must be between $0K and $500K`, flexibility_warning: `Flexibility clause must be between 1 and 5`, tone_warning: `Negotiation tone must be between 1 and 5`, hint_relationship_critical: `Relationship health is critical. The union may walk away from negotiations.`, hint_low_agreement: `Agreement quality is low. Look for integrative trades — bundle safety with flexibility.`, hint_hardline_warning: `A hardline approach is damaging the relationship. Consider a more collaborative tone.`, hint_strong_round: `Strong round! Keep balancing cost containment with relationship building.`, hint_safety_low: `Safety investment is low. After recent incidents, the union will not accept a weak safety package.`, col_phase: `Phase`, col_wage: `Wage Offer (%)`, col_safety: `Safety ($K)`, col_flexibility: `Flexibility`, col_tone: `Tone`, col_relationship: `Relationship`, col_laborscore: `LaborScore`, r1Desc: 'The current CBA at Plasticos del Valle expires in 45 days. As management, you must set your initial negotiating position.<br><br><strong>Context:</strong> The company ($280M revenue, 1,200 unionized workers) needs a production flexibility clause to compete with imports. The union has filed a pliego de peticiones demanding a 12% wage increase and improved safety standards after two workplace incidents.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Set your opening wage offer, safety investment budget, flexibility clause strength, and negotiation tone. This round establishes your BATNA and credibility.', r2Desc: 'Both sides have exchanged opening positions. The union opened at 12% wage increase, $400K safety investment, and rejected any flexibility clause.<br><br><strong>Context:</strong> The gap between positions is significant but not unusual. Your tone and willingness to explore interests (rather than defend positions) will determine whether the negotiation moves toward integrative bargaining or hardens into a distributive fight.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Adjust your position based on the union response. Consider what trades might be possible.', r3Desc: 'Negotiations have entered the substantive phase. Both sides have moved from opening positions but remain apart on key issues.<br><br><strong>Context:</strong> The union has signaled willingness to discuss flexibility if safety investment is substantial. This is a potential integrative trade: management gets flexibility, union gets safety. But the wage gap remains the hardest issue.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Develop a package proposal that bundles trades across multiple issues. Consider whether to request a mediator.', r4Desc: 'This is the final round. You must present your best and final offer. If the union accepts, you have a new CBA. If rejected, the dispute goes to binding arbitration where neither party controls the outcome.<br><br><strong>Context:</strong> Arbitration in Colombia typically splits the difference on wages but can be unpredictable on non-monetary issues. Your BATNA (arbitration) is your alternative — but the relationship cost of arbitration is high.<br><br><strong>Your task:</strong> Submit your final offer. Balance cost containment with agreement quality and relationship preservation.', ev_intel_report: 'Your HR team has obtained informal intelligence: the union leadership is divided. The president favors a collaborative approach, but the vice-president is pushing for a hard line. A moderate opening may exploit this division.', ev_board_pressure: 'The Board of Directors has communicated that total CBA cost increases above 8% of current labor costs will require a special board vote. This constrains your flexibility on wages.', ev_wildcat_action: 'CRISIS: A spontaneous work slowdown has begun in Department 4. Production is down 30% in that unit. The union denies involvement but has not condemned it. How you respond will affect both the negotiation and operational continuity.', ev_media_leak: 'CRISIS: The union opening position has been leaked to El Tiempo newspaper. The headline reads: Workers at Plasticos del Valle demand living wages amid record profits. Public pressure is mounting on management.', ev_safety_incident: 'BREAKING: A minor chemical spill has occurred in Plant B during the morning shift. Two workers treated for skin irritation. The union has called an emergency meeting. Safety investment just became the top priority at the table.', ev_mediator_offer: 'The Ministry of Labor has offered to provide a mediator at no cost to either party. Accepting mediation signals willingness to compromise but may slow the process. The arbitration deadline is in 15 days.', ev_strike_threat: 'The union membership has voted to authorize a strike if no agreement is reached. The vote was 78% in favor. A strike would cost approximately $1.2M per week in lost production.', ev_competitor_deal: 'A competitor in Medellin just settled their CBA at 9.5% wage increase with strong flexibility provisions. Both sides are aware of this benchmark. It provides a credible reference point for settlement.', perf_beginner: 'Beginner Negotiator', perf_skilled: 'Skilled Negotiator', perf_expert: 'Expert Negotiator', insight_relationship_high: 'Strong relationship preservation — this CBA will hold.', insight_relationship_low: 'The relationship is damaged. Even with an agreement, expect work-to-rule and grievances.', insight_agreement_high: 'High agreement quality — integrative trades created mutual value.', insight_agreement_low: 'Agreement leaves value on the table. Explore more trades between safety and flexibility.', insight_cost_high: 'CBA costs are high. The board may require a special vote for approval.', insight_cost_low: 'Cost containment was effective while maintaining reasonable terms.', chart_score_label: 'Round LaborScore' }, es: { title: `LaborDesk — Negociación Colectiva`, subtitle: `Plásticos del V